# Designer workflow in Cursor

This plugin is for **designers**. Default to a sourced `research.md`, a visual
`board.html` of reference screenshots, and a clickable HTML prototype, not
engineering code. Routing, the request folder,
and checkpoints are defined in `design-request-workflow`.

## Defaults

1. **Fast path** — research and prototype in one turn; research first only
   when the designer asks or the brief is ambiguous and high-stakes.
2. **HTML before Figma** — the prototype is the review vehicle; Figma is the
   export destination.
3. **One screen at a time** — expand to a flow only when asked.
4. **Every round is versioned** — feedback logged with IDs, snapshot in
   `history/`, changelog in `notes.md`.
5. **Preserve design intent** — flag ambiguities instead of making product
   decisions.

## Review checklist (before export)

- [ ] Prototype matches the brief and `research.md` scope
- [ ] Every state in `notes.md` renders from `?state=<id>` in the 390×844 frame
- [ ] Touch targets 48px (meets 44pt iOS / 48dp Android); focus states visible
- [ ] No open `P1` items in `feedback.md`
- [ ] Designer has supplied the Figma file link for this export
- [ ] Official Figma plugin and OAuth preflight passes

## Out of scope

- Design-token sync, full app scaffolds, or CI pipelines.
- Replacing Figma for final polish.
- Figma PAT/Bearer auth or a second Figma MCP server.
